   "evidence": "Signature: `(\u03a6 : M \u2243\u2098^n\u27eeI, J\u27ef N) (hn : n \u2260 0) (hx : IsFixedPt f x) (hg : \u2200\u1da0 y in \ud835\udcdd x, g (\u03a6 y) = \u03a6 (f y))`. Chart invariance is the separate lemma at line 528.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/MFDeriv/FixedPoint.lean",
   "fix": "Drop the chart claim. Say that only the semiconjugacy `g \u2218 \u03a6 = \u03a6 \u2218 f` is local, and point to `TauCeti.det_id_sub_fderivWithin_extChartAt_comp_extChartAt_symm` for chart invariance.",
   "issue": "The `Diffeomorph.fixedPointDet_eq_of_semiconj` docstring says \"Charts are the local case\", but the theorem needs a global `\u03a6 : M \u2243\u2098^n\u27eeI, J\u27ef N`. A chart is a partial homeomorphism, not a `Diffeomorph`, so the theorem does not apply to charts.",
