  {
   "evidence": "`theorem fixedPointSign_iterate ... (hk : fixedPointDet I f^[k] x \u2260 0)`. `fixedPointSign_of_nonpos` gives `-1` when the determinant is `0`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/MFDeriv/FixedPoint.lean",
   "fix": "Add the hypothesis in both places, e.g. \"at a fixed point where `det (1 - d(f^[k])_x) \u2260 0`, the sign of `f^[k]` is ...\".",
   "issue": "The module docstring says that at any fixed point with differential `D` the sign of `f^[k]` is `(-1)^i\u208a * (-1)^((k+1)i\u208b)`. `fixedPointSign_iterate` needs `fixedPointDet I f^[k] x \u2260 0`. When the determinant is `0` the sign is `-1` by definition, while the formula can give `+1`. The section docstring at lines 596\u2013597 makes the same unconditional claim (\"at a fixed point the signs of the iterates `f^[k]` are determined by the real eigenvalues\").",
